.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH murmuration 1  "murmuration 0.2.0" 
.SH NAME
murmuration \- Starlings at dusk, in your terminal.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmurmuration\fR [\fB\-\-analyze\fR] [\fB\-\-turns\fR] [\fB\-\-agitation\fR] [\fB\-\-probe\fR] [\fB\-\-zigzag\-k\fR] [\fB\-\-turning\fR] [\fB\-\-falcon\fR] [\fB\-\-colors\fR] [\fB\-\-screensaver\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-arc\fR] [\fB\-\-arc\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-birds\fR] [\fB\-\-seed\fR] [\fB\-\-turn\-side\fR] [\fB\-\-turn\-angle\fR] [\fB\-\-turn\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-turn\-min\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starlings at dusk, in your terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-analyze\fR \fI<SECONDS>\fR
Run headless for this many simulated seconds, printing flock statistics once per second, then exit
.TP
\fB\-\-turns\fR
Run the forced\-turn experiment headless, report the fitted wave speed and R², then exit
.TP
\fB\-\-agitation\fR
Run the agitation\-wave experiment (falcon attack) headless and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-probe\fR
Run the part\-D probe (2000 birds, seed 0, four minutes) and print the metrics that catch the "looks wrong" failures, then exit
.TP
\fB\-\-zigzag\-k\fR \fI<ZIGZAG_K>\fR [default: 2]
Copying threshold k for the zigzag wave (1–7)
.TP
\fB\-\-turning\fR \fI<TURNING>\fR [default: base]
Turning model: base (banked) or inertial (review C7)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
base: The bank tracks `atan(a_lat/g)` with a first\-order lag
.IP \(bu 2
inertial: The bank *rate* has momentum, after the inertial spin model (Cavagna et al. 2015): once a bird starts to roll it keeps rolling (review C7)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-falcon\fR
A falcon hunts from the start
.TP
\fB\-\-colors\fR \fI<COLORS>\fR [default: auto]
Colour handling
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Detect from the environment
.IP \(bu 2
truecolor: 24\-bit colour
.IP \(bu 2
ansi256: Nearest of the 256 xterm colours
.IP \(bu 2
none: Plain braille, no colour
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-screensaver\fR
Exit on any key press or mouse movement
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Do not capture the mouse (no mouse falcon, no exit\-on\-move)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-arc\fR
Hold the display phase (no evening arc)
.TP
\fB\-\-arc\-minutes\fR \fI<ARC_MINUTES>\fR [default: 15]
Length of one evening, in minutes
.TP
\fB\-\-birds\fR \fI<BIRDS>\fR
Number of birds [default: from the terminal size, 4000–8000]
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fI<SEED>\fR
Random seed for the evening
.TP
\fB\-\-turn\-side\fR \fI<TURN_SIDE>\fR [default: 100]
Forced\-turn experiment: birds disturbed
.TP
\fB\-\-turn\-angle\fR \fI<TURN_ANGLE>\fR [default: 0.8]
Forced\-turn experiment: imposed heading change, in radians
.TP
\fB\-\-turn\-window\fR \fI<TURN_WINDOW>\fR [default: 2]
Forced\-turn experiment: seconds to simulate after the disturbance
.TP
\fB\-\-turn\-min\fR \fI<TURN_MIN>\fR [default: 0.3]
Forced\-turn experiment: minimum local heading change to include a bird, in radians
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0
